x86_64-windows  clang compiles this against Microsoft's own <initializer_list>, whose default constructor it emits as `??0?$initializer_list@H@std@@QEAA@XZ`; cxx1's <initializer_list> has the same constructor and emits nothing for it, nothing here calling it. A header difference, not a mangling one - every name both emit agrees. x86_64-linux and arm64-darwin are compared on the Mac: this box's clang has no headers for those targets.
